00:00:02.389 --> 00:00:04.630 align:start position:0%
the wreckage of a plane which crashed  with 22 people on board has been located  in the himalayan mountains in nepal  rescuers have so far recovered 14 bodies  from the crash site the plane was  carrying locals and tourists to a  mountain town  photos from deep in the himalayas  confirmed the worst for the missing  flight  the wreckage was discovered in the early  morning a day after the small plane went  missing  multiple bodies have been recovered but  bad weather and the remote location have  made accessing the site difficult  the flight from pakara to the mountain  town of johnson is a popular one with  tourists it normally only takes about 20  minutes  but air traffic control lost contact  with the aircraft shortly after takeoff  now authorities have confirmed that an  accident occurred about five minutes  before the plane was due to land  experts are still assessing the cause of  the crash  the flight seems to have collided with a  big rock on the hill  the twin otter plane similar to the one  shown here was carrying 22 people  including three crew members  the aircraft is operated by tara air  among the 19 passengers are two german  nationals four indians and 13 nepali  citizens  for the families waiting anxiously for  news the discovery of the crash has  realized their worst fears  unpredictable mountain weather and  remote airport locations means that  plane crashes in nepal are not  infrequent
 

